From ff563e2d3e5d0deeefaa7c7d60fc4bd15eb3445e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 06:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests/checkasm: add swr_rematrix and swr_audio_convert
 coverage

swresample's rematrix mixers and sample format converters had no checkasm
oracle (only FATE end-to-end), so their SIMD paths could never be checked
in isolation. Two new tests, both built on REAL library contexts like
swr_resample.c so the function pointers, coefficient tables and calling
contract are the library's own:

swr_rematrix: an SwrContext per case (same in/out rate, internal_sample_fmt
pinned to S16P or FLTP, custom matrix via swr_set_matrix before swr_init)
and the kernel taken off s->mix_1_1_simd / mix_2_1_simd when the arch init
set one, else the C mix_1_1_f / mix_2_1_f; call_ref gets native_matrix and
call_new native_simd_matrix, since the two tables differ by design (x86 and
PPC pre-scale the int16 coefficients per row). Cases: mix_1_1 and mix_2_1
with plain (|coef| < 1) and clip (>1 gain, the *_clip_s16 C variant)
matrices whose coefficients are k/2^m so the pre-scaled table is exact,
plus the mix6to2 / mix8to2 whole-matrix special cases (default 5.1/7.1 ->
stereo, off s->mix_any_f, any length 1..100). Every pointer is swept over
all 16-byte residues -- real callers hand these kernels user buffers at
arbitrary sample offsets -- and every output plane sits between random
guard bytes that are compared afterwards, so out-of-window writes fail.
S16P is compared bit-exactly, FLTP within 1e-6 (SIMD may contract the
two-product sum differently from the compiler's C).

swr_audio_convert: AudioConvert contexts for every ordered pair of
{S16,S16P,S32,S32P,FLT,FLTP} at 1, 2 and 6 channels (planar only at 1,
where the library forces planar). ctx->simd_f has no C twin, so a
test-local reference with the simd signature replays swri_audio_convert()'s
per-channel conv_f calls and is registered in the C pass; a SIMD pass
registers ctx->simd_f, and pairs without a kernel skip automatically. The
same-layout pairs are called per plane with the element count the library
passes (frames, or frames*channels when packed), pack/unpack once with the
full NULL-terminated pointer arrays, frames a multiple of 16 (the library's
len & ~15). Aligned buffers only (kernels may set the simd_align_mask).
Everything is compared bit-exactly with guards, except float->int16 on
ARM/AArch64 where the existing NEON kernel is known to round differently
from lrintf (truncate to 31-bit fixed then round-half-up narrowing) and
gets a +-1 LSB tolerance.

Written for the PPC AltiVec kernels that follow, but arch-neutral: on x86
they exercise the existing SSE/AVX rematrix and audio_convert asm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VY6bhpLDBYqo84Hbm2ewdh
